# =============================================================================
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT allowlist.
#
# This working tree is a live retail SimCity 3000 install with RE work layered
# on top. The vast majority of it (game binaries, a decrypted iOS app, 63k+
# extracted sprites, the full Ghidra decompilation of EA/Maxis code) MUST NEVER
# be published. This repo ships only our own original work: tools + notes.
#
# The rule below ignores EVERYTHING, then re-includes an explicit allowlist.
# A careless `git add -A` therefore cannot leak assets: anything not named here
# stays ignored. Verify with `git ls-files` before every push.
# =============================================================================

# 1) Ignore everything at the repo root.
/*

# 2) Root files we publish (our own work).
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/HANDOFF.md
!/ROADMAP.md
# The live board: open work by mod/feature, plus the serial game-run queue. Added 2026-08-24,
# same class as ROADMAP/HANDOFF (our own prose, no game bytes). CLAUDE.md stays UNPUBLISHED
# by design, so its pointer at this file is local-only.
!/BOARD.md
!/UNCERTAINTIES.md
!/STUBS.md
!/DEFERRED.md
# Who is working in this repo concurrently, and the rules for sharing the trackers.
# Added 2026-08-17 when three sessions were writing functions.csv at once.
!/SESSIONS.md
!/functions.csv

# 2b) verify/ — the experiment PROTOCOLS and their OUTCOMES, never their artifacts.
#     The READMEs describe how a test is built and what each outcome means. The RESULTS files
#     record what actually happened. Both are prose written by us; the artifacts next to them
#     are derived GAME DATA (copies of shipped cities, an extracted .ini) and must never reach
#     a public repo.
#     Same per-directory shape as re/analysis below: every level denied, then specific
#     filenames re-included, so a NEW subdirectory added later is denied by default.
#
#     RESULTS.md added 2026-08-18. Until then only the READMEs were published, which meant
#     ROADMAP.md and HANDOFF.md both cited verify/city_load_test/RESULTS.md and
#     verify/loose_file_test/ARM3_RESULTS.md as the evidence for T1 and the SYS.PAK writer
#     while neither file was in the repo — the protocols were public and every outcome was
#     local-only. The second pattern catches the ARM3_RESULTS.md style prefix.
#     These are markdown notes and contain no game bytes: hashes, offsets and observations only.
!/verify/
/verify/*
!/verify/*/
/verify/*/*
!/verify/*/README.md
!/verify/*/RESULTS.md
!/verify/*/*RESULTS.md
!/verify/*/RESULTS_*.md
!/verify/*/PRE.md
!/verify/*/*PRE.md

# 3) Re-include the re/ tree, then re-ignore everything inside it.
!/re/
/re/*

# 4) re/tools — Python tools only.
!/re/tools/
/re/tools/*
!/re/tools/*.py
# 4b) re/tools/netmod — the network-modding suite package (netcat etc.), Python only.
#     Its catalog/HTML/PNG output goes to re/netcat_out/ (ignored by /re/*): game art never published.
!/re/tools/netmod/
/re/tools/netmod/*
!/re/tools/netmod/*.py
# netpack (2026-10-13): the manifest JSON Schema, and the example packages' manifest + README ONLY. Examples derive
# their art from the stock pieces at build time; a PNG, DAT or IXF in a package folder is game art and stays ignored.
!/re/tools/netmod/netpack.schema.json
# artkit (2026-10-13): the Blender calibration (numbers only) and the example packages' art RECIPES (compositor JSON:
# the art is built from the stock frames at build time, never shipped).
!/re/tools/netmod/netart_calib.json
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/
/re/tools/netmod/examples/*
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/
/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/*
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/manifest.json
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/README.md
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/recipe.json
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/layout.json
# lanekit (2026-10-13): lane specs are text descriptions (side, slot, curve key), no game art
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/*.lanes.json
# roundabout2 (2026-10-13): netpaint plans are geometry + parameters; colours come from the game at build time
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/paint.json
# roundabout4 (2026-10-14): the closed-quarter plan and recipe (JSON parameters, no game art)
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/paint_*.json
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/recipe_*.json
# hwlight (2026-10-21): the lit-twin id list of a highway package (piece -> twin ids, no game art)
!/re/tools/netmod/examples/*/lit_twins.json

# 5) re/scripts — .py / .ps1 / .java only.
#    Explicitly NOT the .log / .txt Ghidra run artifacts (absolute-path leaks)
#    and NOT the stubs/ output directories.
!/re/scripts/
/re/scripts/*
!/re/scripts/*.py
!/re/scripts/*.ps1
!/re/scripts/*.java

# 6) re/analysis — Markdown only. Excludes the stray *.csv data dumps
#    (functions_raw_1203.csv at top level, formats/gvf_keys.csv one level down).
#    Each directory level is denied explicitly, then only its *.md re-included.
#    A NEW subdirectory added later is denied by default (safe failure mode).
!/re/analysis/
/re/analysis/*
!/re/analysis/*.md
!/re/analysis/formats/
/re/analysis/formats/*
!/re/analysis/formats/*.md

# session briefs, one per mod (tools/notes only, no game content)
!/PROMPTS.md
